    "field": "Climate network analysis",
    "problem": "The atmospheric mechanisms causing extreme rainfall in the eastern Central Andes are not sufficiently resolved, and existing weather models fail to reproduce the specific propagation of these events, thus preventing the development of an effective early warning system.",
    "method": "We propose a framework to predict extreme rainfall events by introducing the concept of network divergence on directed networks, which are derived from a non-linear synchronization measure applied to satellite-derived rainfall data.",
    "task": "The task is to develop a framework using a complex networks approach on satellite-derived rainfall data to predict extreme flood events in the eastern Central Andes of South America.",
