            "paragraph": "We employ the 3-hourly real-time satellite product TRMM 3B42V7 RT27 for the time period from 2001 to 2013. To forecast extreme rainfall events in the ECA, we define prediction times as SESA times with a low-pressure anomaly in northwestern Argentina (geopotential height anomalies less than 10 m in white polygon in Fig. 3a; this condition is abbreviated as GPH in Table 1).",
